First, you need to set up Firebase in your Laravel project. This involves creating a Firebase project, enabling the Authentication service, and obtaining the Firebase configuration.

Once Firebase is set up, you can use the Firebase Admin SDK in Laravel to manage user authentication. The Admin SDK allows you to create, manage, and delete users, as well as verify ID tokens.

To authenticate a guest user, you can use the Firebase Admin SDK to create a new user with a custom token. This token can then be sent to the client, where it can be used to authenticate the user with Firebase.

Here's an example of how to create a custom token for a guest user:

