{
    public function createGuestUser()
    {
        $factory = (new Factory())->withServiceAccount('path/to/serviceAccountKey.json');
        $auth = $factory->createAuth();

        $customToken = $auth->createCustomToken('guest-user-id');

        return response()->json(['token' => $customToken]);
    }
}

In this example, we're using the Firebase Admin SDK to create a custom token for a user with the ID 'guest-user-id'. This token can then be used by the client to authenticate with Firebase.

On the client side, you can use the Firebase SDK to sign in with the custom token:

