This will authenticate the user with Firebase using the custom token generated by the Laravel backend.

It's important to note that custom tokens are only valid for a limited time (usually 1 hour) and should not be used for long-term authentication. For long-term authentication, you should use Firebase's built-in authentication methods, such as email/password or OAuth.

In addition to creating custom tokens, you can also use the Firebase Admin SDK to manage user data, such as creating user records in the Firebase Realtime Database or Cloud Firestore.

